{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1427151-snarled-silk-pankratist-silliness","id":1427151,"title":"Snarled-Silk Pankratist Silliness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-03T09:29:05-08:00","id":1427151,"title":"Snarled-Silk Pankratist Silliness","content":"I think I've figured out a way to get infinite damage using The Distaff, and specifically the evocation Snarled-Silk Pankratist.<br /> The key is craft dice tricks charms.<br /> <br /> The steps are:<br /> Grapple the enemy with The Distaff.<br /> Activate Snarled-Silk Pankratist.<br /> Use the following charms on the join battle roll: Fate-Shifting Solar Arete (repurchased), Flawless Handiwork Method (repurchased), Supreme Masterwork Focus (Repurchased Twice), First Movement of the Dmeiruge, Divine Inspiration Technique, and the bonus of a Jewel of the Rabbit's Foot.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Assuming a perfectly average 30 dice (3 of each number), you will </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Treat every 2 and 3 as a 10.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Reroll every 1, 6 and 10 (15 dice)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Get 3 each of 7, 8, 9 (change 3 failed dice to 10s, rerolling it)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Get 9 10s (change 3 failed dice to 10s, rerolling it)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Get 6 dice altered to 10s (all the failures, they would change more failures to 10s but we run out)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Earn 48 successes, every 3 of which generates a non-charm die (16 more dice).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">You rerolled a total of 21 dice, and generated 16 new ones.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Every 30 dice rolled allows you to roll on average 37 more dice.<br /> Obviously, any given set of dice might do worse than this, but if you do ok on the first few set you'll eventually be rolling so many dice that the chance of failing drops dramatically.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This means that, depending on your initial number of dice, there is some probability p such that for any number, there is at least a p chance of reaching at least that many successes. If you start with enough dice (5 wits, 5 craft, a specialty, a 1-point stunt, a full excellency, and the exceptional equipment bonus should do it), you have a very good chance of dealing infinite damage, for a reasonable definition of \u201cchance of dealing infinite damage\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> Once your pankratist has arbitrarily large initiative, they can simply make a decisive savaging attack<br /> <br /> I also ran a java program simulating this, obviously I didn't run it for infinite time but it seemed to work.<br /> <br /> This has a few obvious flaws, such as needed to successfully grapple first, requiring you to roll an infinite number of dice, a small but non-zero chance of stopping with a finite number of successes, and the fact that your Storyteller may object.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23597,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","user":"autXautY","date":". 12-03-2020, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T10:20:51-08:00","id":1427164,"title":"","content":"Haven't read Distaff in a while but how are you grappling first THEN rolling join battle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T10:25:38-08:00","id":1427165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1427151-snarled-silk-pankratist-silliness?p=1427164#post1427164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't read Distaff in a while but how are you grappling first THEN rolling join battle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Silk-Snarled Pankratist allows you to construct a golem made out of silk that takes over the grapple for you.<br /> It is rolled into battle with a wits+craft(weaving) roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T10:28:25-08:00","id":1427166,"title":"","content":"Reading the evocation, it reads to me that the construct couldn't benefit from charms for the Join Battle because it specifically mentions &quot;unmodified pools&quot; a few words later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T11:03:39-08:00","id":1427171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1427151-snarled-silk-pankratist-silliness?p=1427166#post1427166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading the evocation, it reads to me that the construct couldn't benefit from charms for the Join Battle because it specifically mentions &quot;unmodified pools&quot; a few words later.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a plausible interpretation. I'm not sure if the unmodified pools clause applies to the join battle roll or not.<br /> Magma Kraken is rolled into battle with a roll that doesn't match it's other pools, but Prince of the Fallen Tower is rolled into battle with it's own pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T11:46:59-08:00","id":1427177,"title":"","content":"Your odds of dealing infinite damage are precisely zero, for the not very interesting reason that in order to progress to the 'make a decisive savaging attack' step and actually deal any damage at all, the 'absurd exploding join battle of doom' step has to have terminated, and it can only terminate with a finite natural number of successes. <br /> <br /> Your odds of killing whoever you are grappling are rather good, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26536-elenian","name":"Elenian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T12:20:41-08:00","id":1427183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elenian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1427151-snarled-silk-pankratist-silliness?p=1427177#post1427177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your odds of dealing infinite damage are precisely zero, for the not very interesting reason that in order to progress to the 'make a decisive savaging attack' step and actually deal any damage at all, the 'absurd exploding join battle of doom' step has to have terminated, and it can only terminate with a finite natural number of successes.<br /> <br /> Your odds of killing whoever you are grappling are rather good, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>This really gets into the question of the definition of &quot;odds&quot; and &quot;infinite&quot;. And &quot;dealing damage&quot;, since if you spend 1000 years rolling join battle you'll never actually get to dealing damage.<br /> The more technical definition I'd stick by is: &quot;<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">there is some probability p such that for any number, there is at least a p chance of reaching at least that many successes&quot;</span></span><br /> That is, there is at least a 60% chance of hitting 10 successes, and at least 60% chance of hitting 100, and at least 60% chance of hitting 1000, and so on, for any number you care to name. (assuming you start with some reasonable number of dice)<br /> <br /> Since First Movement of the Demiurge says you &quot;may&quot; replace a non-success die with a 10, I guess the term &quot;arbitrarily large&quot; is accurate, since you can stop doing that once you hit enough initiative and the cycle will slowly finish.<br /> <br /> Arguably the bigger limit is that I don't know of a way to grapple giant creatures as a Solar using Melee, so this can only be used to grapple human-sized enemies, who are less likely to need more than thirty level of damage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T16:52:24-08:00","id":1427219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1427151-snarled-silk-pankratist-silliness?p=1427183#post1427183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This really gets into the question of the definition of &quot;odds&quot; and &quot;infinite&quot;. And &quot;dealing damage&quot;, since if you spend 1000 years rolling join battle you'll never actually get to dealing damage.<br /> The more technical definition I'd stick by is: &quot;<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">there is some probability p such that for any number, there is at least a p chance of reaching at least that many successes&quot;</span></span><br /> That is, there is at least a 60% chance of hitting 10 successes, and at least 60% chance of hitting 100, and at least 60% chance of hitting 1000, and so on, for any number you care to name. (assuming you start with some reasonable number of dice)<br /> <br /> Since First Movement of the Demiurge says you &quot;may&quot; replace a non-success die with a 10, I guess the term &quot;arbitrarily large&quot; is accurate, since you can stop doing that once you hit enough initiative and the cycle will slowly finish.<br /> <br /> Arguably the bigger limit is that I don't know of a way to grapple giant creatures as a Solar using Melee, so this can only be used to grapple human-sized enemies, who are less likely to need more than thirty level of damage</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, like if for some reason you knew you needed to deal 100 damage you could do it with this combo, and if you knew you needed to do 1,000 damage you could also do it with this combo, or 10,000, or whatever. There are other combos that could possibly hit these damage levels, but only with vanishingly small probabilities, but this one has a substantial chance - hard to calculate, but probably at least 60% or so, as you note. <br /> <br /> Why you NEED to do so much damage is between you and your Storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T13:21:24-08:00","id":1427296,"title":"","content":"Ask the Devs has supported using charms to enhance the join battle roll of Snarled-Silk Pankratist. However, they pointed out that some charms specify craft projects. Of the ones I'm using, it looks like only Supreme Masterwork Focus is ruled out, but that does weaken this.<br /> It drops to 42 successes/30 dice, which means 14 extra dice, for 35 dice per 30 dice. Still enough, but the chances of failure did increase.<br /> I probably should re-run the calculations to figure out what the minimum probability is for different starting dice pools.<br /> <br /> The other inapplicable charms are bright-forging prana, and inspiration-renewing vigor+horizon unveiling insight (only make sense if there's a terminus anyways)<br /> Experiential Conjuring of True Void can't be used for basic projects, but says it can be used after an (attribute+craft) roll with no mention of it being for a project, so I think it would be ok.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}